            <Placemark id="4098">
                <name>Reitbrooker Mühle </name>
                <description>
                category  : See_Vierland and the marshes &lt;br&gt;
                address  :   &lt;br&gt;
                url  :   &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Built in 1870, this windmill is next to the Reitbrooker Mühlenbrücke (&quot;mill bridge&quot;). This is a so-called &quot;Galerieholländer&quot; windmill; a square two-story stone building with a wooden octagon building on the top. It was used until as a windmill 1938 or 1939, and became a protected building in 1942. It still functions as a mill, albeit not a wind powered one. When the fodder shop is open, you can also see the mill from the inside. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="4097">
                    <coordinates>10.1719143,53.4671862,0.0</coordinates>
